<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanatana Goswami</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1488–<a href="/years/1558">1558</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sanatana Goswami was a theologian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaudiya-vaishnavism">Gaudiya Vaishnavism</a>, one of the six Goswamis of Vrindavan and elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupa-goswami">Rupa Goswami</a>. He served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-husain-shah">Alauddin Husain Shah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> as a minister, was imprisoned when he tried to resign, and escaped to join Chaitanya. At Vrindavan he wrote <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> works on Vaishnava ritual and theology, including the Brihad-bhagavatamrita, and helped restore its sacred sites.</p></div>
